														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1226512">
									

<p>I definitely believe the original myth, whatever it is, is a solid basis for an SCP. That being said, I feel like the execution was off. Tonally, this feels too much like a tale and not enough like an SCP. It also really just didn't grab me that much; I felt like some of the details were a bit extraneous, like the whole &quot;bodies disapearing when the ghosts disappear&quot; thing. I don't know, this one just didn't really work for me.</p>
<p>Also, you left in a few XX's throughout, and I got really confused with some of the phrasing in the containment procedures and early on in the description. I get that you were trying to keep us in the dark about what the SCP actually was until about half way down the page, but the result was that you used so much vague wording and pronouns that I completely lost track of what I was reading.</p>

							</div>

								
